dsv41 patch 0072 (21.10.2026): background decode pause. In use (VLLM_DSV41_BG_PAUSE_PRIO=10).
Why: with patch 0071 a background request next to a foreground one verifies no drafts, but its anchor row still brings
the routed experts of a second context into every round (the profile of 21.10.: a round costs 24.8 ms fixed + 3.6 ms per
request + 2.8 ms per live row, the live-row part almost entirely routed experts). In our setup the background requests
are the memory service's (priority 10 from our proxy) and they overlap nearly every interactive request, so the
interactive stream decoded at 43 (prose) / 66 (code) tok/s instead of ~54 / ~83.
How: in the scheduler's loop over the running requests, a decoding request with priority >= P is skipped while a
request with priority < P is running (the same kind of skip as vLLM's V2 + PP decode cadence a few lines above). It keeps
its KV blocks and its drafts and is scheduled again as soon as no foreground request runs. Prefill chunks are left to
the prefill throttle (patch 0031). P comes from VLLM_DSV41_BG_PAUSE_PRIO (0 = off); the depth file
(VLLM_DSPARK_DEPTH_FILE) token "bgpause=<P>" overrides it live, read by the scheduler every 256 steps (a line without the
token falls back to the environment value). Outputs are unchanged: a paused request only waits.
Measured (21.10.2026, GB10, image v20, live through the depth file, against 0071 with bg=0; one foreground request with
priority 0, 384 tokens, T = 0, next to one or two background streams with priority 10, two runs per cell): foreground
prose + 1 / 2 background 42.9 / 34.4 -> 53.9 / 53.8 tok/s, code + 1 / 2 background 66.4 / 57.5 -> 83.3 / 83.2 tok/s
(+25 ... +56 %, geometric mean +38 %); first token unchanged (0.23-0.29 s); background 0 tokens/s while the foreground
decodes; no errors. Against the state before 0071: prose + 2 background 22.2 -> 53.8, code + 2 background 40.2 -> 83.2.
Switch: VLLM_DSV41_BG_PAUSE_PRIO=<P> (requests with priority >= P count as background), depth-file token bgpause=<P>.
